*/*.pdf
*.ipynb

# The gateway image is what the organisers deploy, with settings we cannot see, so it must be safe as built
# (adr/0001-gateway-image-is-the-security-boundary.md). gateway/tests/test_deployment.py checks these rules.

# The demo routes sign mandates for anyone who asks. Left out, they cannot be switched on;
# docker-compose.demo.yaml mounts the file back in for the local walkthrough.
gateway/demo.py

# Only the state the running gateway reads. Never the issuer's, an agent's or a person's private key, a mandate,
# the nonce database or the record. A mounted state folder hides this one anyway.
gateway/state/*
!gateway/state/.gitkeep
!gateway/state/trusted_list.json
!gateway/state/status_list.json
!gateway/state/status_list.jwt
!gateway/state/people.json
!gateway/state/people.jwt
!gateway/state/gateway_key.pem
